From: Xperia Hikari Linux Project <hikari-linux@localhost>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 13:05:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: route MSM8x60 DSI through its pixel RCG

Sony's MSM8x60 DSI implementation does not feed the video pixel stream
through the MDP PIXEL_CC/MD/NS registers.  It programs the dedicated DSI
pixel RCG at 0x130/0x134/0x138 from the DSI PLL instead.  The working Hikari
vendor kernel uses the 209.018880 MHz PLL output with the RCG's bypass
pre-divider set to three, producing 69.672960 MHz.

The Hikari DTS currently connects the DSI host's pixel input to
MDP_PIXEL_CLK.  That leaves the real DSI pixel RCG stopped; on hardware the
DSI video engine remains idle and neither DSI nor MDP produces scanout
interrupts even though all video timing registers are correct.

Describe the vendor divider using the table-driven RCG operations.  The board
DTS can then connect the host to DSI_PIXEL_CLK and select the DSI PLL for the
dedicated DSI pixel RCG.  Using a pure pre-divider for the 1/3 ratio also
matches the vendor programming model, which deliberately bypasses the M/N
counter when M is one.

Signed-off-by: Xperia Hikari Linux Project <hikari-linux@localhost>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8660.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8660.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8660.c
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8660.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8660.c
@@ -668,6 +668,12 @@ static struct clk_branch dsi1_esc_clk = {
 	},
 };
 
+static const struct freq_tbl clk_tbl_dsi1_pixel[] = {
+	/* Hikari MDV22: 209.018880 MHz DSI PLL / 3 = 69.672960 MHz. */
+	{ .freq = 69673000, .src = P_DSI1_PLL_DSICLK, .pre_div = 3 },
+	{ }
+};
+
 static struct clk_rcg dsi1_pixel_src = {
 	.ns_reg = 0x0138,
 	.md_reg = 0x0134,
@@ -687,6 +693,7 @@ static struct clk_rcg dsi1_pixel_src = {
 		.src_sel_shift = 0,
 		.parent_map = mmcc_pxo_dsi2_dsi1_map,
 	},
+	.freq_tbl = clk_tbl_dsi1_pixel,
 	.clkr = {
 		.enable_reg = 0x0130,
 		.enable_mask = BIT(2),
@@ -695,8 +702,7 @@ static struct clk_rcg dsi1_pixel_src = {
 			.name = "dsi1_pixel_src",
 			.parent_data = mmcc_pxo_dsi2_dsi1,
 			.num_parents = ARRAY_SIZE(mmcc_pxo_dsi2_dsi1),
-			.ops = &clk_rcg_pixel_ops,
-			.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
+			.ops = &clk_rcg_ops,
 		},
 	},
 };
